  message: "F3 noise reduction landed across Phase 1 PR-A/B/C (PRs #3699, #3700, #3701). Filter 1 (skip is_resolved=False edges in _compute_external_potential, ADR-0028 sibling field) + Filter 3 (composition fix for self-prefixed dst names, eliminates re.re.MULTILINE / ast.ast.Name double-prepend) shipped in PR-A. PR-B pinned the io-boundaries --json envelope at schema_version 1.0 with property tests on the top-level shape. PR-C added the closed-world stdlib gating substrate: IoBoundaryCatalog.stdlib_modules / stdlib_prefixes / stdlib_module_completeness fields, is_stdlib_module() / is_stdlib_module_complete() methods, F3 Filter 2 in _compute_external_potential, the deterministic refresh-stdlib-modules operator script, and 300-module Python 3.12 population with math as the inaugural worked-example closed-world flag. The closed-world surface starts narrow (one module) and expands per future hand audits without further code changes. 100% coverage maintained across all three PRs. Tagging awaits_bakeoff_validation per discipline — the ~4,521-chain F3 Filter 1 reduction claim and the math-flagged Filter 2 cut need bakeoff confirmation on the prospector corpus before stripping the tag."  # 530a
